From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jack O'Regan Kenny <42699197+jackoregankenny@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 19:05:51 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Subway: NYC subway countdown from the MTA's GTFS-Realtime
 feeds

The clock fetches the MTA feeds itself over HTTPS (no server in the loop)
and shows the next trains for up to three lines at one station.

- core/transit: streaming GTFS-RT decoder with fixed state (trips, and
  the Mercury alerts feed), arrival rules, the route table (every line's
  feed, color and bullet), gunzip, and the 32x8 layouts: colored numbers
  in time order, bullets side by side, or one line at a time; red dot for
  an MTA disruption.
- system: the fetch task (one request per feed, gzip through the ESP32
  ROM tinfl, pinned MTA roots, backoff, paused while the display is dark),
  the subway_* script natives, the Subway script app, and first-boot gift
  defaults (New York time, 12 h, volume 0, off when pitch dark at 1%).
- Tests against real MTA snapshots, cross-checked with Google's
  gtfs-realtime-bindings.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
